  "all_ingredients_flat": "potatoes, beetroot, frozen veggies mix, carrots, beans, corn, green peas, green chillies, ginger piece, red bell pepper, cilantro, mint leaves, Ginger Garlic Paste, turmeric powder, black pepper powder, red chili powder, Chaat Masala, amchur powder, salt, chia seeds, hempseed, Ezekiel 4:9 bread, sooji (upma rava or farina), whole wheat flour, water, bell peppers",
  "instructions": "Veggies: In a thick bottom pan, cook frozen veggies on medium heat for 5-10 mins. Then add beetroot, bell peppers, green chillies, ginger and all the spices except Ginger Garlic Paste. Cook for 3-4 minutes. Then add boiled potato pieces. Mix well & mash with a potato masher or a thick spoon. Now add Ginger Garlic Paste. Mix well and cook for a minute. Add greens, cilantro and mint. Mix well and switch off the stove. Don't cook after adding greens. Let mixture cool before making patties.\nBread Crumbs [optional]: Toast bread slices to make them hard. Grind them along with chia seeds and hemp seeds. Mix sooji rava.\nMake patties: Make round patties using the vegetable mix. If using bread crumbs, dip the patty in the water and flour mixture, then dip in bread crumbs mix to evenly coat the patty with bread crumbs. Freeze these patties for 1 hour before cooking them.\nCook patties: Cook both sides for 5 minutes each on medium heat in a pan. Then air fry for 4 minutes on each side.",
  "cooking_methods": [
    "saute",
    "mash",
    "toast",
    "blend",
    "no-cook",
    "freeze",
    "air-fry"
  ],
  "serving_suggestion": "Garnish like microgreens, red onions, tomatoes & homemade ketchup.",
  "notes": "Bread Crumbs [optional]. A recipe with WHOLE GRAINS (corn, Ezekiel 4:9 bread), BEANS (green peas, Ezekiel 4:9 bread), TUBERS (potato), RAINBOW VEGGIES (beetroot, carrot, bell pepper...), NUTS & SEEDS (chia seeds, hempseed), HERBS & SPICES (various).",
